Topic :Difference Between Useradd and adduser in linux

1.useradd prerna

Creates the user but does not ask for password, full name, etc. You must manually set password using passwd prerna.

2.adduser prerna

Starts an interactive setup: asks for password, full name, room number, etc.

3.Example:

>Useradd (Manual)

# Create a user with home directory

sudo useradd -m prerna

# Set password for the user

sudo passwd prerna

# Add to a group

sudo useradd -m -G devops prerna

>Adduser(Interactive)

# Create a user with prompts

sudo adduser prerna

You’ll be prompted for:

 • Password,Fullname etc

>Memory Tip:-adduser adds nicely, useradd needs manual flags.


